We compare the rating quality in paper commenting in Figure \ref{fig:pe_Commenting}. We observe that \ours achieves higher review quality than the experts. Moreover, we find that paper rating does not necessarily have a higher paper quality than paper commenting. 
In paper commenting, each paper is first evaluated by the evaluation agent, who offers detailed comments or suggestions for improvement. These comments can convince screening agents to reject the paper. We assume that this comment-based procedure can make screening AI scientists consider more aspects of the $\mathbf{x}$, which is a major difference from the rating procedure.
