\subsubsection{In-Context Learning}
\label{sec:ablation_studies_in_context}

In paper commenting, we increase the number of in-context examples and find it can improve the performance as shown in Figure \ref{fig:ablation_in_context}. In comparison, we show the paper rating where the number of in-context examples is fixed as 4 for commenting. In the paper rating scenario, MAAC outperforms other methods. In the paper commenting scenario, we find that IPO performs well in the MAAC training stage, because IPO is a training method similar to MAAC (both use reinforcement learning). However, IPO is still worse than MAAC because IPO does not consider the different perspectives of reviewers. In the paper commenting scenario, IPO gets 0.72 in paper quality and 0.0232 in the MAAC training. MAAC improves the paper rating and commenting from 0.65 to 0.72 and 0.017 to 0.0232, respectively.

