\subsubsection{Learning Methods}
\label{sec:ablation_studies_different_learning_method}

In Figure \ref{fig:ablation_MARL}, we explore the effectiveness of different MARL methods in optimizing our AI scientists. We consider three different MAAC methods: MADDPG (multi-agent Deep Deterministic Policy Gradient) \citep{Hinton06}, MAPPO (multi-agent Proximal Policy Optimization) \citep{hu2022lora}, and multi-agent actor-critic \citep{lowe2017multi}. In addition, we consider two optimization methods: preference optimization \citep{rafailov2023direct} and iterative length-regularized direct preference optimization (IPD) \citep{liu2024iterativelengthregularizeddirectpreference}. Preference optimization is a reinforcement learning method that involves using dataset of positive and negative examples to optimize a policy for a positive or negative review. IPD is based on Direct Preference Optimization (DPO) that trains a reward model by maximizing the loss, which involves modeling a reward distribution to approximate human preferences. In Figure \ref{fig:ablation_MARL}, we find that MAAC outperforms other methods in the paper rating scenario. 


