In Figure \ref{fig:methods_overview}, we show that \ours competes with GPT-4-Turbo in the same team. In this section, we study the qualitative effects of this competitive preference optimization. 
In the paper rating scenario, \ours learns to imitate different experts with diverse perspectives on paper quality. 
\ours competes with other AI scientists for the same paper and selects the best AI scientist that outperforms the others. We find that the AI scientists can provide constructive feedback for weak points in weak papers. Moreover, our AI scientists can sometimes disagree with experts due to the diversity of paper topics. This disagreement leads to more comprehensive and objective feedback compared to a single expert.

