In this paper, we draw inspiration from human scientific discovery for inspiration to develop an innovative AI agent that can autonomously collaborate with others and collectively advance scientific progress. We propose an innovative iterative multi agent reinforcement learning approach, drawing inspiration from human scientific discovery. This approach integrates three key elements: 1) collaborative agents, including proposal agents (AS), design agents (RA), review agents (AR), all tailored to effectively generate and evaluate scientific ideas; 2) an iterative exploration framework that enables agents to iteratively update their roles and concurrently explore and improve the exploration strategy, allowing for deeper optimization in each stage of discovery; 3) fine-tuning capabilities that allow agents to learn from reviews and enhance their performance, facilitating iterative optimization within each stage and collective evolution across stages.
Experiments on discovery tasks related to chemistry, which have traditionally relied heavily on human input, demonstrate that our proposed method can effectively support autonomous scientific discovery in a manner similar to human collaboration. Our results also reveal that the fine-tuned review agent can provide reviews that are not only factually accurate but also aligned with human expectations and preferences. This research is a step towards the development of an autonomous AI agent learning to discover knowledge and contribute to scientific discovery in a manner akin to humans. 

