\section{Limitations}

Our work has three main limitations. First, we focus on reviewing quality, and there's a need for more human annotations or alternative evaluation methods. Second, there's a scope for improvement in the review quality analysis at duty and ethics awareness. Third, there's a need for further improvement on challenging examples. One solution is to integrate AI scientists~\citep{lu2024ai}, use reinforcement learning with AI feedback~\citep{shinn2023reflexion,zhang2024generative} or verifiers~\citep{weng-etal-2023-large} to enhance performance.






\section{Conclusion}

In this work, we introduce \method{}, an AI-assisted reviewer LLM (Large Language Model) aimed to perform the full peer reviewing process to emulate the role-playing capabilities of human reviewers. We conduct a comprehensive quality analysis to assess the effectiveness and efficiency of \method{}. Extensive results show that \method{} outperforms human reviews and OpenAI GPT-4 Turbo in both general and quality assessment, outperforms Author-ASSIST-revised in recommendations, and performs competitively with Author-ASSIST and Author-ASSIST-revisd in review quality, demonstrating the effectiveness and efficiency of our approach. 





